WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.489
The AI Profile Builder writes the instructions of an AI profile with you.

00:00:05.489 --> 00:00:09.012
You play the person the AI will talk to, tell it what it

00:00:09.012 --> 00:00:12.080
got wrong, and it rewrites its own instructions.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.001
This video shows why it exists, how it works, and how to build,

00:00:16.001 --> 00:00:18.160
test and save a profile with it.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.121
An AI profile that holds a conversation on its own, such as an

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:32.700
automated text message or phone call, behaves only as well as its system message.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:38.755
Writing that message by hand means guessing at every situation, trying it in

00:00:38.755 --> 00:00:41.990
a chat, and editing it again, over and over.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:47.780
And a fix for one reply can quietly break another reply that used to work.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.027
The Profile Builder turns this around.

00:00:51.027 --> 00:00:54.998
You play the conversation, say what the AI got wrong, and the AI

00:00:54.998 --> 00:00:58.970
rewrites its own instructions until it behaves the way you want.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.337
A session is a chat with a coach beside it.

00:01:06.337 --> 00:01:10.990
You role-play in text or by voice, and give feedback on any reply.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.950
The coach reads your comment, the conversation, and every earlier piece of feedback,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.440
including the replies you threw away.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.650
It rewrites the system message and, when needed, parameters such as the temperature.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:29.974
Every rewrite is kept as a revision you can restore, and Replay checks

00:01:29.974 --> 00:01:32.140
that earlier fixes still hold.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:38.290
When the assistant behaves the way you want, you save the result as an AI profile.

00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:45.685
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profile Builder.

00:01:45.685 --> 00:01:47.903
Your sessions are listed here.

00:01:48.355 --> 00:01:51.536
New Session starts with empty instructions.

00:01:51.536 --> 00:01:56.275
To improve an AI profile you already have, open the menu beside it.

00:01:56.726 --> 00:01:59.725
Pick the profile, and start the session.

00:01:59.725 --> 00:02:04.746
It begins with the profile's instructions, model, parameters and tools.

00:02:05.196 --> 00:02:07.059
The page has three parts.

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:11.146
The settings on the left hold the instructions and parameters.

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:16.008
The chat in the middle is where you play the person the AI talks to.

00:02:16.008 --> 00:02:18.749
Here, a patient texting a dental office.

00:02:19.201 --> 00:02:23.560
And the Builder panel on the right holds your feedback, the revisions, the

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.631
replay, and the finished result.

00:02:29.823 --> 00:02:32.533
Write what the patient would say, and send it.

00:02:35.558 --> 00:02:37.985
The assistant answers with a price.

00:02:37.985 --> 00:02:41.477
But this office doesn't quote prices by text message:

00:02:41.477 --> 00:02:43.548
the front desk confirms them.

00:02:44.012 --> 00:02:46.187
Under the reply, click Feedback.

00:02:46.187 --> 00:02:48.762
The reply moves into the Builder panel.

00:02:49.222 --> 00:02:51.692
Write what was wrong, in your own words.

00:02:54.366 --> 00:03:00.626
Feedback and regenerate rewrites the instructions, then answers the same message again with them.

00:03:01.076 --> 00:03:05.091
The new rule is in the system instructions, and the new reply leaves

00:03:05.091 --> 00:03:06.936
the price to the front desk.

00:03:07.388 --> 00:03:09.918
When a reply is right, click Looks good.

00:03:09.918 --> 00:03:12.118
Later rewrites keep that behavior.

00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:17.532
Every piece of feedback stays in this list, with the replies you rejected.

00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:22.308
Each rewrite reads all of it, so fixing one thing doesn't undo another.

00:03:26.497 --> 00:03:32.207
The Revisions tab keeps every version of the instructions, with what changed and why.

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:38.129
Expand a revision to read its system message, and restore it to make it current again.

00:03:38.581 --> 00:03:43.299
On the Replay tab, Run replay answers every message you gave feedback on

00:03:43.299 --> 00:03:45.901
again, with the current instructions.

00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:50.902
Then it checks each answer against your feedback, and marks it Pass or

00:03:50.902 --> 00:03:52.579
Fail, with the reason.

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:56.771
Tools aren't used during a replay, so nothing is sent or booked.

00:04:00.972 --> 00:04:05.093
On the Finish tab, the opening message is what the assistant is told

00:04:05.093 --> 00:04:08.992
when it starts a conversation itself, such as an automated text.

00:04:09.444 --> 00:04:13.768
The coach deployment is the model that rewrites the instructions.

00:04:13.768 --> 00:04:16.264
A capable model writes better ones.

00:04:16.717 --> 00:04:21.258
Copy the system message, save the result as a new AI profile, or

00:04:21.258 --> 00:04:24.567
update the profile this session started from.

00:04:25.017 --> 00:04:30.707
The profile opens with the instructions you built, ready for automated messages and calls.

00:04:32.707 --> 00:04:37.626
The AI Profile Builder turns the replies you don't want into instructions that hold.

00:04:37.626 --> 00:04:39.047
Thanks for watching.

